<!-- People › Positions & recruiting (design-people §5, §1.2; impl-people P4): the seats, the job classes they are of and the pay
    grades. The menu group of design §1.2: Positions (the default subscreen, Staffing/Positions), Job classes and Pay grades;
    PositionDetail and JobClassDetail are opened from a row. P16 (design §5, §13): Openings, Applicants (ApplicantPipeline) and
    Interviews (InterviewsCalendar, Commons' calendar with its EventDetail), ApplicantDetail opened from a card or an interview:
    a recruiter (PEOPLE_RECRUIT_VIEW of the employer) reads the openings and applications, an interviewer the applications of their
    panels and their own scorecards (mantle.humanres.RecruitingServices). Every People user
    opens them: what each sees is what Mantle's services admit (positions to HR, recruiting, payroll and configuration readers of
    the employer and to a manager for the departments they lead; job classes and grade names to every staff reader; a grade's
    amounts to payroll alone, mantle.humanres.PayrollSetupServices), and HR editors change positions and classes, payroll grades.
    P17 (design §5 OfferDetail, §15): OfferDetail, an offer of employment opened from ApplicantDetail, a notice or the hire wizard
    (a recruiter's, HR's and payroll's of the employer, and its approver's: mantle.humanres.RecruitingServices), and OfferLetter, its
    letter's print, both out of the menu. -->
<screen xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="http://moqui.org/xsd/xml-screen-3.xsd"
        default-menu-title="Positions &amp; recruiting" default-menu-index="6" menu-image="sym_o_work" menu-image-type="icon">
    <subscreens default-item="Positions">
        <!-- Positions (menu index 1), JobClasses (2) and PayGrades (3) are files under Staffing/, with PositionDetail and
            JobClassDetail out of the menu; P16: Openings (4), ApplicantPipeline (5, "Applicants") and InterviewsCalendar (6,
            "Interviews"), with ApplicantDetail and InterviewsCalendarTui out of the menu; P17: OfferDetail and OfferLetter out of the
            menu -->
    </subscreens>
    <widgets>
        <subscreens-active/>
    </widgets>
</screen>
